femticPy patch 0002-read_MTdata-snap-before-copy

Rationale: read_MTdata snapped near-duplicate frequencies in edi_data after data_Z/data_VTF had been copied, so snapped values never reached data_Z and prep_data silently dropped those rows; snap first.

--- a/src/femticPy.py
+++ b/src/femticPy.py
@@ -137,6 +137,22 @@
                     print ('    reading %s'%edi_file)
                     #read edi file
                     edi_data, site_id, coord = MTtools.read(edi_file_path)
+                    # data.append([site_id, edi_data])
+                    # site_ids.append(site_id)
+                    # coords.append(coord)
+                    # list all the existing frequencies in the dataset
+                    # [patch 0002] snap near-duplicate frequencies BEFORE data_Z / data_VTF are copied from
+                    # edi_data, so the snapped values reach the tables that prep_data filters on
+                    for freq in range(len(edi_data['FREQ'].values)):
+                        if not edi_data['FREQ'].values[freq] in freq_list:
+                            if freq == 0:
+                                freq_list.append(edi_data['FREQ'].values[freq])
+                            else:
+                                if min(np.abs(np.log10(freq_list) - np.log10(edi_data['FREQ'].values[freq]))) < 0.01:
+                                    idx = (np.abs(freq_list - edi_data['FREQ'].values[freq])).argmin()
+                                    edi_data.loc[freq, "FREQ"] = freq_list[idx]
+                                else:
+                                    freq_list.append(edi_data['FREQ'].values[freq])
                     
 
                     
